### ─── INTERVIEWS ─────────────────────────────────

### Demarrer une session
# @name startInterview
POST {{baseUrl}}/interviews/start
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "type": "tech_stack",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "stack_focus": "Laravel",
  "duration_min": 30
}

###

@session_id = {{startInterview.response.body.session.id}}
@question_id = {{startInterview.response.body.session.current_question.id}}

### Repondre a une question
POST {{baseUrl}}/interviews/{{session_id}}/respond
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "question_id": "{{question_id}}",
  "text_answer": "Un Service Provider dans Laravel est une classe qui bootstrap les services de l application. Il contient deux methodes principales : register() pour lier les services au container, et boot() pour les actions apres enregistrement.",
  "code_submitted": "<?php\nclass AppServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider\n{\n    public function register(): void {}\n    public function boot(): void {}\n}",
  "language": "php"
}

###

### Demander un indice
POST {{baseUrl}}/interviews/{{session_id}}/hint
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "question_id": "{{question_id}}",
  "partial_answer": "Je sais que c est lie au container..."
}

###

### Terminer la session
POST {{baseUrl}}/interviews/{{session_id}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Rapport de session
GET {{baseUrl}}/interviews/{{session_id}}/report
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Historique interviews
GET {{baseUrl}}/interviews
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

